<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  App export job (docs/DAILY_PIPELINE.md, "App export job"). NOT loaded by anything in the repo: the maintainer installs it by hand.
    install:    cp ops/launchd/local.nba.app-export.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/ && launchctl bootstrap gui/$(id -u) ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.nba.app-export.plist && launchctl kickstart -k gui/$(id -u)/local.nba.app-export
    (the kickstart writes a first heartbeat at once; without it the watchdog alerts app-export:stale until the first slot has run)
    uninstall:  launchctl bootout gui/$(id -u)/local.nba.app-export && rm ~/Library/LaunchAgents/local.nba.app-export.plist
  Two slots an hour, :05 and :35, 12-23 on the schedule clock (the first after the morning job, 08:00; ~2 h when the Drive upload is slow), so they
  fall between the pretip runs (:20 + a few minutes, :50). After today's first export a slot rebuilds only when a pretip run has ended since
  the last build and a game has not tipped; otherwise it is a one-second no-op. launchd evaluates the calendar on the same clock as the other jobs (data/ops/schedule_tz);
  keep the hours and minute in step with JOBS["app-export"] in nba/ops/watchdog.py (tests/ops/test_app_export.py checks it).
  Launched through uv, never /bin/sh: TCC blocks sh from reading ~/Downloads (exit 126 stopped every job once).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>local.nba.app-export</string>
  <key>WorkingDirectory</key><string>/Users/devin/Downloads/nba-prediction</string>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/uv</string><string>run</string><string>--no-sync</string>
    <string>python</string><string>-m</string><string>nba.ops.app_export</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>12</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>5</integer></dict>
    <dict><key>Hour</key><integer>12</integer><key>Minute</key><integer>35</integer></dict>
